### Description

I noticed many invalid expression when checking for a zero elements in a collection.

Here is explanation

```
List<string> items = null;

if(items?.Count == 0)
{
    // This will evaluate false since null does not equals 0.
}

if(items?.Any() ==false)
{
    // This will evaluate false since items is null. which is translated to items != null && items.Count == 1
}
if(items == null || items.Count == 0)
{
    // This will evaluate true since items either null OR is not null and it's count is 0.
}

if(items?.Count > 0)
{
    // This check is okay because null items will return false and if the Count is 0 will also false.
}
```


